hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1101","Chapter on a man training his horse and the virtue of archery, 1140 - al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Bayruti informed us that his father informed him, he said: Ibn Jabir narrated to us, he said: Abu Sallam narrated to me, he said: Khalid, that is Ibn Yazid, narrated to me, who said: I was an archer, and Uqbah al-Juhani would call me saying: Come out with us, O Khalid, to shoot. One day I was late for him, so he said: Come, let me tell you what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me, and let me say to you what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah admits three people to Paradise by a single arrow: its maker who seeks good in making it, the one who shoots it, and the one who hands the arrows to him. Shoot and ride, and that you shoot is dearer to me than that you ride. There is no idle pastime except in three: a man training his horse, his playing with his wife, and his shooting with his bow and arrows. Whoever abandons archery after learning it out of disinterest in it, it is a blessing he has been ungrateful for."
